WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
TFSA holders eyeing 5.9% yields on Enbridge after the stocks dip below $66. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 245. Friday's closes, a simulated manualife hold, and co-founder IPO sales, then the Fortis Review, tools, and the record. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.220
financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:45.268
S&amp;P 500 finished Friday at 7,297, up 1.6%. The NASDAQ composite closed Friday at 24,130,

00:00:45.928 --> 00:00:54.628
up 2.3%. A year-to-date gain of 3.85% and 7.85% since the practice portfolio opened on March 16,

00:00:54.628 --> 00:01:03.548
2026. TSX Composite finished Friday at 34,840, up 1.2 percent, with gold and copper

00:01:03.548 --> 00:01:09.408
miners leading the move. Chicago Fed President Austin Goolsbee flagged opaque AI financing

00:01:09.408 --> 00:01:14.688
structures, noting that non-transparent arrangements typically signal issues rather than healthy

00:01:14.688 --> 00:01:21.188
ones. 14 days ago, we picked STT on valuation after positive post-earnings drift, and it

00:01:21.188 --> 00:01:23.648
It closed down 8% when rotation shifted.

00:01:24.228 --> 00:01:29.348
Bank of Canada and Federal Reserve decisions remain the macro anchors, with markets pricing

00:01:29.348 --> 00:01:31.728
modest easing into early 2027.

00:01:32.685 --> 00:01:37.805
Manualife Financial pays a quarterly dividend of 48.5 cents at $60 a share.

00:01:38.405 --> 00:01:44.125
Motley Fool Canada calculates, for a 3.23% yield that a TFSA keeps in full.

00:01:44.805 --> 00:01:51.325
MetLife's 2.4% gross yield keeps only 85% of that cash after the 15% US withholding.

00:01:51.325 --> 00:01:56.765
that a TFSA cannot recover through foreign tax credits, so the American name needs roughly

00:01:56.765 --> 00:02:01.245
3.8% gross to match the net Canadian payout on the same $10,000.

00:02:02.045 --> 00:02:09.225
You hold $10,000 of that US insurer in a TFSA and a Canadian peer yields 3.23%.

00:02:09.225 --> 00:02:13.545
Do you keep the US name for a different geography or switch for cash in the account?

00:02:14.225 --> 00:02:16.245
Here's how the withholding math answers it.

00:02:16.665 --> 00:02:20.585
Open the brokerage, pull the current dividend and the current price on each candidate.

00:02:20.585 --> 00:02:26.305
it, cut any U.S. ordinary dividend by 15%, then compare the net dollars that actually

00:02:26.305 --> 00:02:28.085
land per 10,000 invested.

00:02:28.505 --> 00:02:33.545
15% withholding is a cover charge at the door of a U.S. concert that your Canadian season

00:02:33.545 --> 00:02:34.665
pass cannot refund.

00:02:35.365 --> 00:02:38.405
The headline yield on the poster is not the cash in your pocket.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:43.685
The method works when income is the priority and currency swings are secondary, and it

00:02:43.685 --> 00:02:48.845
failed for many in 2025 when U.S. growth stocks outpaced the after-tax yield gap.

00:02:48.845 --> 00:02:54.685
Check the exact withholding rate on your broker's tax report before you commit capital, because the

00:02:54.685 --> 00:02:58.925
posted statutory cut is the starting point, not always the line on the slip.

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:05.265
Manualife's Asia earnings growth and record core earnings of $1.24 per share in the latest

00:03:05.265 --> 00:03:10.705
quarter are the earnings support behind that distribution. Enbridge has 31 consecutive years

00:03:10.705 --> 00:03:15.945
of dividend increases and $38 billion in secured capital projects expected to lift

00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:22.385
distributable cash flow about 5% annually, while BCE's larger prior cut is the cautionary

00:03:22.385 --> 00:03:27.665
case for chasing yield without testing payout sustainability. The technique therefore favors

00:03:27.665 --> 00:03:33.885
Canadian names when the goal is maximum after tax cash inside a TFSA, rather than total return.

00:03:34.605 --> 00:03:41.643
Remember, gross yield is a brochure. Net cash is the paycheck. Manually financial, ticker MFC

00:03:41.643 --> 00:03:46.843
on the TSX, is the simulated weekly hold that puts that dividend yield comparison to

00:03:46.843 --> 00:03:48.223
work on a Canadian insurer.

00:03:48.743 --> 00:03:52.343
And this is a simulated trade for learning purposes with no real money.

00:03:52.863 --> 00:03:57.703
It enters that Monday's open under the published rules and is judged against the NASDAQ over

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:58.983
its own five sessions.

00:03:59.543 --> 00:04:03.343
A share's structure in financials, strategy family dividend income.

00:04:04.023 --> 00:04:08.703
Price sits below recent highs but above the 200-day moving average on the daily chart,

00:04:08.703 --> 00:04:13.783
start, with volume near the 20-day average, so the moving average filter is intact, and

00:04:13.783 --> 00:04:16.203
the volume filter is only average, not a spike.

00:04:16.863 --> 00:04:22.983
The stop loss is 8% below entry, which caps the loss at $80 on the $1,000 position if

00:04:22.983 --> 00:04:29.143
that level prints intraday, and the target is plus 2% to plus 5% over the 5-session window

00:04:29.143 --> 00:04:30.523
if yield support holds.

00:04:31.183 --> 00:04:36.583
Confidence is medium, dividend history and earnings momentum align, but sector rotation

00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:42.623
signals remain mixed, which is two factors in one real uncertainty, not a high conviction stack.

00:04:43.403 --> 00:04:47.963
Invalidation is the next release showing quarterly core earnings per share below the prior year

00:04:47.963 --> 00:04:53.783
level. That is the thesis breaker name before the simulated money is at risk, and I am keeping it

00:04:53.783 --> 00:04:58.403
on the earnings print rather than on a price line, because that is the test that has been matching

00:04:58.403 --> 00:05:04.363
these medium confidence dividend holds. Rotation can still punish a clean income setup even when the

00:05:04.363 --> 00:05:09.683
yield math is clean, so the 8% stop is the hard cap and the earnings in validation is

00:05:09.683 --> 00:05:10.703
the fundamental one.

00:05:11.568 --> 00:05:15.228
Several $1,000 simulated positions run side by side.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:21.828
This one is a five session hold from Monday's open, stop or Friday's horizon, no discretionary

00:05:21.828 --> 00:05:22.608
exit in between.

00:05:23.268 --> 00:05:28.968
Fortis, ticker FTS, was the last weekly hold, a defensive dividend entry on a low beta

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:31.628
utility with steady capital spending visibility.

00:05:31.628 --> 00:05:35.768
Similarly, simulated from Monday's open to Friday's close across five sessions.

00:05:36.148 --> 00:05:43.408
We simulated buying it at $84 at the Monday open and exited at $83.69 at Friday's close,

00:05:43.928 --> 00:05:49.948
a loss of 0.37%, or $3.69 on the $1,000 position.

00:05:50.628 --> 00:05:56.888
NASDAQ lost 0.58% over the same five sessions, so the trade lost money and still posted

00:05:56.888 --> 00:05:59.988
plus 0.21% alpha versus that window.

00:05:59.988 --> 00:06:05.628
Stated confidence was medium, the stated invalidation was any quarter where adjusted earnings

00:06:05.628 --> 00:06:10.128
fall below the prior year level on the next release, and that print never mattered.

00:06:10.628 --> 00:06:13.148
The 8% stop below entry was not reached.

00:06:13.728 --> 00:06:19.068
Medium fit the mixed yield support against rotation pressure, the stop was never tested, and

00:06:19.068 --> 00:06:21.548
the earnings tied in validation stayed the right switch.

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:25.968
This didn't work as a dollar gain, and the adjustment is to keep judging these holds

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:30.628
on alpha against the NASDAQ window, rather than on whether the utility ticked up.

00:06:31.578 --> 00:06:35.478
Unusual Wales surfaces large options trades with filters for size,

00:06:36.038 --> 00:06:38.198
unusual activity, and dark pool prints,

00:06:38.618 --> 00:06:42.878
so a retail screen can see institutional positioning before the cash market moves.

00:06:43.438 --> 00:06:45.378
The free tier supplies basic scans,

00:06:45.978 --> 00:06:49.318
the paid tier adds historical GEX and market tied data,

00:06:49.718 --> 00:06:55.538
which is the step you run when you want flow that often precedes earnings or merger headlines on an event-driven name.

00:06:55.538 --> 00:07:01.858
Pacific Economic Development Canada's regional tariff response initiative supplies non-repeable

00:07:01.858 --> 00:07:07.698
funding to support wages that affected facilities, including $2 million awarded to CONFX for

00:07:07.698 --> 00:07:08.798
its Mackenzie sawmill.

00:07:09.178 --> 00:07:14.078
That award is tied to maintaining employment, which can stabilize cash flow and reduce

00:07:14.078 --> 00:07:19.298
dilution risk for a smaller forestry operator, and the latest check offsets tariff-related

00:07:19.298 --> 00:07:21.118
cost pressure at that one location.

00:07:21.118 --> 00:07:26.998
Investors tracking Canadian forestry or manufacturing names can read the recipient lists and application

00:07:26.998 --> 00:07:30.638
details on the Pacific Economic Development Canada site directly.

00:07:31.378 --> 00:07:35.958
