Dynacore's board approved a monthly dividend of 1.333 cents Canadian per share, payable

00:08:03.512 --> 00:08:09.092
December 17th to shareholders of record December 9th, continuing the established monthly schedule.

00:08:09.772 --> 00:08:14.752
DNG is the ticker if a TFSA watchlist needs a small monthly pair with that distribution

00:08:14.752 --> 00:08:15.352
history.

00:08:15.352 --> 00:08:23.928
Sable's first Zorro holes, 15 of them totaling 2673 meters, confirmed copper continuity at Zorro

00:08:23.928 --> 00:08:29.568
North to about 200 meters depth, with grades at depth comparable to surface sampling and several

00:08:29.568 --> 00:08:38.188
intercepts between 0.10% and 0.25% copper. SAE is the name to park on a watch list until follow-up

00:08:38.188 --> 00:08:45.360
assay batches arrive, not an exploration allocation on this batch alone. Generation mining closed a $100

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:50.140
million dollar convertible note offering, unsecured subordinated notes split 50

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:54.920
million dollars each to Canada Growth Fund Incorporated and Canada Infrastructure Bank,

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:58.660
proceeds for project development without immediate equity dilution.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:04.660
GENM is the balance sheet watch for whether that capital actually cuts near-term financing risk.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:11.610
The rules-based matched window alpha versus NASDAQ averages plus 0.78% per trade

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:18.070
across 61 trades. 36 of those 61 positions beat the index over their own windows, for

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:25.150
a cumulative loss of $305.50 across the positions. A result that remains early with a T statistic

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:33.510
of plus 1.04. The full history since March 2026 shows 112 trades with a 51% win rate and

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:41.290
cumulative P&amp;L of minus $814.62. Those rules are fixed five session holds, entry at the

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:47.650
next open, stop or horizon exits, no discretionary exits, and the AI overlay is still treating

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:52.510
mixed rotation around dividend names as a medium confidence input rather than a green light.

00:09:53.483 --> 00:09:59.623
Anthropic co-founders sold identical blocks at $83, unusual whales laid out, and the shares

00:09:59.623 --> 00:10:04.343
then traded below that level within days of the initial public offering, or IPO.

00:10:04.943 --> 00:10:09.823
You bought at the open after that $83 IPO, and watched the price fall through the number

00:10:09.823 --> 00:10:11.543
the insiders had already accepted.

00:10:12.163 --> 00:10:20.383
The seven co-founders each sold 3,378,378 shares at exactly $83 as part of the offering,

00:10:21.043 --> 00:10:26.243
locking in nearly $2 billion total while retaining 98.6% of their holdings.

00:10:26.763 --> 00:10:33.123
Dario Amode and his sister Danyella each sold $280 million worth, matching the identical

00:10:33.123 --> 00:10:35.183
block size sold by every other founder.

00:10:35.183 --> 00:10:40.023
That coordinated sale was disclosed in the offering documents and went to underwriters

00:10:40.023 --> 00:10:45.263
rather than the open market, yet the stock has since traded below the $83 the insiders

00:10:45.263 --> 00:10:45.583
took.

00:10:46.143 --> 00:10:50.963
The identical share count across all seven founders is a pre-planed structure, not

00:10:50.963 --> 00:10:55.423
seven separate moods, and it leaves new shareholders one visible reference point.

00:10:55.983 --> 00:11:00.443
Any sustained trade below that level is the market rejecting the valuation the insiders

00:11:00.443 --> 00:11:01.063
locked in.

00:11:01.063 --> 00:11:05.723
Note the exact insider sale price and share count on the first trading day.

00:11:06.143 --> 00:11:10.903
Then set an alert 5% below it so you see the anchor break instead of discovering it in

00:11:10.903 --> 00:11:11.863
a draw-down review.

00:11:12.383 --> 00:11:17.163
The common misconception is treating every IPO insider sale as routine noise.

00:11:17.763 --> 00:11:22.123
The fix is to treat the disclosed sale price as the first real market test of demand,

00:11:22.683 --> 00:11:27.243
and to size any post IPO position on that test rather than on assumed momentum.

00:11:27.243 --> 00:11:32.043
models and agents covers the AI side daily if you want that tape without the

00:11:32.043 --> 00:11:37.798
equity anchor lesson attached. Open your TFSA holdings list, identify any U.S.

00:11:37.918 --> 00:11:42.898
dividend stock, calculate its net yield after the 15% withholding, and compare

00:11:42.898 --> 00:11:47.698
that figure to a Canadian peer yielding at least 3%. Then write down which name

00:11:47.698 --> 00:11:53.098
delivers more cash per $10,000 invested. Before we wrap, Monday's open is the

00:11:53.098 --> 00:11:57.138
simulated manualife entry, and the first thing I will check on that tape is

